1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,745
Sweetheart, my sister-in-law Joan raised a little

2
00:00:03,745 --> 00:00:06,420
girl who wasn't hers for six years.

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:07,999
Packed her lunches,

4
00:00:07,999 --> 00:00:09,545
sewed her prom dress,

5
00:00:09,545 --> 00:00:12,196
sat up with her through every fever.

6
00:00:12,376 --> 00:00:14,129
And that girl hated her.

7
00:00:14,309 --> 00:00:15,795
For forty years.

8
00:00:15,975 --> 00:00:18,645
She didn't invite Joan to her wedding.

9
00:00:18,825 --> 00:00:21,194
She didn't send a card when Joan's

10
00:00:21,194 --> 00:00:22,099
husband died.

11
00:00:22,279 --> 00:00:24,999
And then, in two thousand fifteen,

12
00:00:24,999 --> 00:00:27,398
she opened a box of Joan's old

13
00:00:27,398 --> 00:00:28,038
diaries.

14
00:00:28,218 --> 00:00:30,352
And she found out what Joan had

15
00:00:30,352 --> 00:00:31,178
been hiding.

16
00:00:31,528 --> 00:00:33,798
Tonight I'm going to tell you the

17
00:00:33,798 --> 00:00:36,068
secret Joan kept for forty years,

18
00:00:36,068 --> 00:00:38,132
why she kept it even though it

19
00:00:38,132 --> 00:00:39,920
cost her that girl's love,

20
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:41,984
and the phone call at three in

21
00:00:41,984 --> 00:00:43,979
the morning, from a hospital,

22
00:00:43,979 --> 00:00:45,217
that ended it all.

23
00:00:45,397 --> 00:00:46,363
Stay with me,

24
00:00:46,363 --> 00:00:48,743
honey, because I was in the room

25
00:00:48,743 --> 00:00:51,643
when they finally saw each other again.

26
00:00:51,992 --> 00:00:54,495
Joan is Harold's younger sister,

27
00:00:54,495 --> 00:00:54,965
honey.

28
00:00:55,145 --> 00:00:56,511
She married late,

29
00:00:56,511 --> 00:00:59,727
at thirty-two, in nineteen seventy-five,

30
00:00:59,727 --> 00:01:01,656
to a widower named Dale,

31
00:01:01,656 --> 00:01:04,229
a quiet man who drove a delivery

32
00:01:04,229 --> 00:01:04,711
truck.

33
00:01:04,891 --> 00:01:06,943
And Dale had a daughter,

34
00:01:06,943 --> 00:01:08,653
Kim, who was twelve.

35
00:01:08,833 --> 00:01:12,507
Dale told everybody that Kim's mother had

36
00:01:12,507 --> 00:01:14,568
died, two years before.

37
00:01:14,748 --> 00:01:17,293
Kim had her mother's picture on her

38
00:01:17,293 --> 00:01:19,473
nightstand, in a silver frame.

39
00:01:19,653 --> 00:01:21,217
And she looked at Joan,

40
00:01:21,217 --> 00:01:22,782
the day of the wedding,

41
00:01:22,782 --> 00:01:24,414
like Joan was a burglar.

42
00:01:24,763 --> 00:01:27,145
It was hard from the very first

43
00:01:27,145 --> 00:01:28,374
day, sweetheart.

44
00:01:28,554 --> 00:01:30,702
Kim wouldn't eat Joan's cooking.

45
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:32,565
She called her that woman.

46
00:01:32,745 --> 00:01:35,051
She said, you're not my mother,

47
00:01:35,051 --> 00:01:36,687
and you never will be,

48
00:01:36,687 --> 00:01:38,249
at least once a week.

49
00:01:38,429 --> 00:01:40,616
When Joan sewed her a dress for

50
00:01:40,616 --> 00:01:42,238
the eighth-grade dance,

51
00:01:42,238 --> 00:01:44,848
Kim cut the sleeves off with scissors

52
00:01:44,848 --> 00:01:46,753
and wore a T-shirt instead.

53
00:01:46,933 --> 00:01:49,801
And Joan never said one word back.

54
00:01:49,981 --> 00:01:51,142
Not one.

55
00:01:51,322 --> 00:01:53,887
I didn't understand it at the time.

56
00:01:54,238 --> 00:01:55,914
I used to tell her,

57
00:01:55,914 --> 00:01:58,826
Joan, that girl needs to hear the

58
00:01:58,826 --> 00:01:59,532
word no.

59
00:01:59,712 --> 00:02:02,242
And Joan would just shake her head

60
00:02:02,242 --> 00:02:03,283
and say, Ruth,

61
00:02:03,283 --> 00:02:04,623
she's lost enough.

62
00:02:04,803 --> 00:02:06,869
Let her be angry at me.

63
00:02:07,049 --> 00:02:08,442
I can take it.

64
00:02:08,622 --> 00:02:10,039
It made me furious,

65
00:02:10,039 --> 00:02:13,693
honey, watching my sister-in-law get treated like

66
00:02:13,693 --> 00:02:15,333
that in her own house.

67
00:02:15,513 --> 00:02:17,160
But Joan had a look in her

68
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:19,693
eyes, like she knew something we didn't.

69
00:02:19,873 --> 00:02:22,367
In a minute I'll tell you what

70
00:02:22,367 --> 00:02:22,949
it was.

71
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:26,469
There was one Christmas I'll never forget,

72
00:02:26,469 --> 00:02:26,922
honey.

73
00:02:27,102 --> 00:02:28,878
Nineteen seventy-seven.

74
00:02:29,058 --> 00:02:30,486
Kim was fourteen.

75
00:02:30,666 --> 00:02:33,143
Joan had saved for months to buy

76
00:02:33,143 --> 00:02:34,691
her a record player,

77
00:02:34,691 --> 00:02:37,013
the one Kim had circled in the

78
00:02:37,013 --> 00:02:38,097
Sears catalog.

79
00:02:38,277 --> 00:02:41,223
And Kim opened it on Christmas morning,

80
00:02:41,223 --> 00:02:42,886
in front of all of us,

81
00:02:42,886 --> 00:02:44,321
looked at the card,

82
00:02:44,321 --> 00:02:47,042
and said, I don't want anything from

83
00:02:47,042 --> 00:02:47,344
you.

84
00:02:47,524 --> 00:02:49,894
And she walked upstairs and left it

85
00:02:49,894 --> 00:02:51,181
there on the floor.

86
00:02:51,361 --> 00:02:54,068
Joan picked up the wrapping paper and

87
00:02:54,068 --> 00:02:55,970
folded it, very carefully.

88
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:58,201
I'll tell you what she wrote that

89
00:02:58,201 --> 00:02:59,320
night in a minute.

90
00:02:59,670 --> 00:03:02,347
Joan started keeping a diary the year

91
00:03:02,347 --> 00:03:03,577
she married Dale,

92
00:03:03,577 --> 00:03:04,012
honey.

93
00:03:04,192 --> 00:03:06,178
Every night, before bed,

94
00:03:06,178 --> 00:03:07,750
she wrote one page,

95
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:09,985
in a little cloth notebook.

96
00:03:10,165 --> 00:03:12,549
She bought a new one every January

97
00:03:12,549 --> 00:03:13,811
at the dime store.

98
00:03:13,991 --> 00:03:16,228
By the time all this happened,

99
00:03:16,228 --> 00:03:17,869
she had forty of them,

100
00:03:17,869 --> 00:03:20,330
in a cardboard box in her closet.

101
00:03:20,510 --> 00:03:22,669
She never let anybody read them.

102
00:03:22,849 --> 00:03:24,312
Not even Dale.

103
00:03:24,492 --> 00:03:26,747
She said, a diary is where you

104
00:03:26,747 --> 00:03:28,927
put the things you can't say.

105
00:03:29,277 --> 00:03:32,586
If Grandma's story is touching your heart,

106
00:03:32,586 --> 00:03:34,714
tap the like button for me,

107
00:03:34,714 --> 00:03:35,581
sweetheart.

108
00:03:35,761 --> 00:03:38,988
It helps more people find these stories.

109
00:03:39,168 --> 00:03:40,874
And Kim grew up,

110
00:03:40,874 --> 00:03:41,514
honey.

111
00:03:41,694 --> 00:03:43,467
She graduated high school,

112
00:03:43,467 --> 00:03:45,513
and she went off to college in

113
00:03:45,513 --> 00:03:48,310
Cleveland, and she called her father once

114
00:03:48,310 --> 00:03:48,787
a week.

115
00:03:48,967 --> 00:03:51,173
She never once asked for Joan.

116
00:03:51,353 --> 00:03:53,806
She married in nineteen eighty-seven,

117
00:03:53,806 --> 00:03:56,127
and she sent the invitation only to

118
00:03:56,127 --> 00:03:56,856
her father.

119
00:03:57,036 --> 00:03:58,685
Dale went alone.

120
00:03:58,865 --> 00:04:01,684
Joan stayed home and wrote in her

121
00:04:01,684 --> 00:04:02,197
diary.

122
00:04:02,547 --> 00:04:05,288
Dale passed in nineteen ninety-eight,

123
00:04:05,288 --> 00:04:06,622
of a heart attack.

124
00:04:06,802 --> 00:04:08,833
And Kim blamed Joan.

125
00:04:09,013 --> 00:04:11,239
She said Joan should have made him

126
00:04:11,239 --> 00:04:12,090
see a doctor.

127
00:04:12,270 --> 00:04:13,268
At the funeral,

128
00:04:13,268 --> 00:04:15,332
she sat on the opposite side of

129
00:04:15,332 --> 00:04:17,662
the church, and she left before the

130
00:04:17,662 --> 00:04:18,261
luncheon.

131
00:04:18,441 --> 00:04:21,332
And for seventeen years after that,

132
00:04:21,332 --> 00:04:24,141
sweetheart, she never called Joan,

133
00:04:24,141 --> 00:04:24,884
not once.

134
00:04:25,064 --> 00:04:26,608
Not on Christmas.

135
00:04:26,788 --> 00:04:28,576
Not on her birthday.

136
00:04:28,756 --> 00:04:31,821
Joan sent a card every Christmas anyway.

137
00:04:32,001 --> 00:04:33,685
They never came back.

138
00:04:33,865 --> 00:04:35,653
But they were never answered.

139
00:04:36,003 --> 00:04:37,483
I asked Joan once,

140
00:04:37,483 --> 00:04:40,197
honey, in about two thousand ten,

141
00:04:40,197 --> 00:04:41,924
sitting on her porch.

142
00:04:42,104 --> 00:04:43,203
I said, Joan,

143
00:04:43,203 --> 00:04:46,840
after everything, don't you hate that girl,

144
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:48,025
just a little?

145
00:04:48,205 --> 00:04:50,503
And Joan looked out at the street

146
00:04:50,503 --> 00:04:51,618
for a long time.

147
00:04:51,798 --> 00:04:52,857
And she said,

148
00:04:52,857 --> 00:04:55,628
Ruth, I've never hated her for one

149
00:04:55,628 --> 00:04:56,198
second.

150
00:04:56,378 --> 00:04:57,748
I just miss her.

151
00:04:57,928 --> 00:04:59,391
Every single day.

152
00:04:59,571 --> 00:05:02,286
Then she changed the subject to her

153
00:05:02,286 --> 00:05:02,984
tomatoes.

154
00:05:03,164 --> 00:05:05,602
I didn't understand that either.

155
00:05:05,782 --> 00:05:07,849
Not until the diaries.

156
00:05:08,199 --> 00:05:10,242
So far, a stepdaughter,

157
00:05:10,242 --> 00:05:11,574
a cut-up dress,

158
00:05:11,574 --> 00:05:13,440
a wedding invitation,

159
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:15,838
and a box of forty diaries.

160
00:05:16,018 --> 00:05:19,111
In November of two thousand fifteen,

161
00:05:19,111 --> 00:05:20,657
Joan had a stroke,

162
00:05:20,657 --> 00:05:21,173
honey.

163
00:05:21,353 --> 00:05:23,001
She was seventy-two.

164
00:05:23,181 --> 00:05:25,399
Her neighbor found her on the kitchen

165
00:05:25,399 --> 00:05:25,759
floor.

166
00:05:25,939 --> 00:05:27,380
And in the hospital,

167
00:05:27,380 --> 00:05:29,902
the doctors said she might not wake

168
00:05:29,902 --> 00:05:30,118
up.

169
00:05:30,298 --> 00:05:33,069
Kim was still listed in Dale's old

170
00:05:33,069 --> 00:05:34,861
papers as next of kin.

171
00:05:35,041 --> 00:05:36,922
So the hospital called her.

172
00:05:37,102 --> 00:05:38,774
At three in the morning.

173
00:05:38,954 --> 00:05:40,022
Stay with me.

174
00:05:40,372 --> 00:05:42,633
Kim drove down from Cleveland,

175
00:05:42,633 --> 00:05:45,348
sweetheart, but she didn't go to the

176
00:05:45,348 --> 00:05:46,478
hospital first.

177
00:05:46,658 --> 00:05:49,018
She went to Joan's house to find

178
00:05:49,018 --> 00:05:50,566
the insurance papers,

179
00:05:50,566 --> 00:05:52,336
because somebody had to.

180
00:05:52,516 --> 00:05:55,337
She told me later she felt nothing.

181
00:05:55,517 --> 00:05:58,640
Like she was handling a stranger's affairs.

182
00:05:58,820 --> 00:06:00,530
And in Joan's closet,

183
00:06:00,530 --> 00:06:02,240
looking for a folder,

184
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:04,927
she knocked over a cardboard box.

185
00:06:05,107 --> 00:06:08,200
And forty little cloth diaries spilled out

186
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,600
all over the floor.

187
00:06:09,950 --> 00:06:12,158
She picked up the first one,

188
00:06:12,158 --> 00:06:12,631
honey.

189
00:06:12,811 --> 00:06:14,785
Nineteen seventy-five.

190
00:06:14,965 --> 00:06:16,853
And it fell open to the week

191
00:06:16,853 --> 00:06:18,135
before the wedding.

192
00:06:18,315 --> 00:06:20,516
And she sat down on the closet

193
00:06:20,516 --> 00:06:22,204
floor, and she read it.

194
00:06:22,384 --> 00:06:25,134
It said, Dale told me the truth

195
00:06:25,134 --> 00:06:25,844
tonight.

196
00:06:26,024 --> 00:06:28,009
Kim's mother didn't die.

197
00:06:28,189 --> 00:06:29,013
She left.

198
00:06:29,193 --> 00:06:31,590
She ran off to California with a

199
00:06:31,590 --> 00:06:33,013
man from the plant,

200
00:06:33,013 --> 00:06:34,810
and she never came back,

201
00:06:34,810 --> 00:06:36,308
and she never wrote,

202
00:06:36,308 --> 00:06:38,330
not even on Kim's birthday.

203
00:06:38,681 --> 00:06:41,171
It said, Dale told Kim her mother

204
00:06:41,171 --> 00:06:44,039
died, because he couldn't bear for her

205
00:06:44,039 --> 00:06:46,680
to know her mother didn't want her.

206
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:48,986
And now I'm going to marry him,

207
00:06:48,986 --> 00:06:50,975
and I'm going to have to keep

208
00:06:50,975 --> 00:06:52,073
that secret too.

209
00:06:52,253 --> 00:06:54,465
That little girl is going to hate

210
00:06:54,465 --> 00:06:57,147
me, because she thinks I'm replacing her

211
00:06:57,147 --> 00:06:57,617
mother.

212
00:06:57,797 --> 00:06:59,737
And I can never tell her the

213
00:06:59,737 --> 00:07:00,153
truth.

214
00:07:00,333 --> 00:07:02,929
Because the truth would break her heart

215
00:07:02,929 --> 00:07:05,059
worse than hating me ever could.

216
00:07:05,239 --> 00:07:06,701
So let her hate me.

217
00:07:07,052 --> 00:07:09,319
Kim told me she read that page

218
00:07:09,319 --> 00:07:11,057
four times, sweetheart.

219
00:07:11,237 --> 00:07:13,393
Then she turned to Christmas,

220
00:07:13,393 --> 00:07:15,103
nineteen seventy-seven.

221
00:07:15,283 --> 00:07:16,816
The record player.

222
00:07:16,996 --> 00:07:18,377
Joan had written,

223
00:07:18,377 --> 00:07:19,921
she didn't want it.

224
00:07:20,101 --> 00:07:21,402
That's all right.

225
00:07:21,582 --> 00:07:23,037
She played it tonight,

226
00:07:23,037 --> 00:07:24,426
though, very quietly,

227
00:07:24,426 --> 00:07:26,609
after she thought we were asleep.

228
00:07:26,789 --> 00:07:28,426
I heard it through the floor.

229
00:07:28,606 --> 00:07:31,516
She played her mother's favorite song,

230
00:07:31,516 --> 00:07:32,588
over and over.

231
00:07:32,768 --> 00:07:34,521
So I'm glad I bought it.

232
00:07:34,701 --> 00:07:36,292
And Kim remembered.

233
00:07:36,472 --> 00:07:38,449
She had played that song,

234
00:07:38,449 --> 00:07:41,139
all night, crying into her pillow.

235
00:07:41,489 --> 00:07:43,177
Kim read all night,

236
00:07:43,177 --> 00:07:46,109
sweetheart, on that closet floor.

237
00:07:46,289 --> 00:07:48,310
Forty years of pages.

238
00:07:48,490 --> 00:07:51,243
And every single page had her name

239
00:07:51,243 --> 00:07:51,729
in it.

240
00:07:51,909 --> 00:07:53,123
Kim had a cold,

241
00:07:53,123 --> 00:07:54,419
I made her soup,

242
00:07:54,419 --> 00:07:56,038
she wouldn't eat it,

243
00:07:56,038 --> 00:07:58,062
but she ate the crackers.

244
00:07:58,242 --> 00:08:00,947
Kim cut the sleeves off the dress.

245
00:08:01,127 --> 00:08:03,786
I think she looked beautiful anyway.

246
00:08:03,966 --> 00:08:05,998
Kim got an A in chemistry.

247
00:08:06,178 --> 00:08:08,199
I'm so proud I could burst,

248
00:08:08,199 --> 00:08:09,772
but I can't tell her,

249
00:08:09,772 --> 00:08:11,344
she'll just be angry.

250
00:08:11,694 --> 00:08:14,122
And then, nineteen eighty-one,

251
00:08:14,122 --> 00:08:14,608
honey.

252
00:08:14,788 --> 00:08:18,294
Joan had been cleaning houses on Saturdays.

253
00:08:18,474 --> 00:08:20,912
Kim's father thought it was for pin

254
00:08:20,912 --> 00:08:21,330
money.

255
00:08:21,510 --> 00:08:22,427
It wasn't.

256
00:08:22,607 --> 00:08:25,624
Every dollar went into a savings account,

257
00:08:25,624 --> 00:08:26,948
under Dale's name,

258
00:08:26,948 --> 00:08:28,273
for Kim's college.

259
00:08:28,453 --> 00:08:31,553
Eleven thousand dollars over six years.

260
00:08:31,733 --> 00:08:34,230
Kim had always thought her father paid

261
00:08:34,230 --> 00:08:35,018
for college.

262
00:08:35,198 --> 00:08:36,487
He couldn't have.

263
00:08:36,667 --> 00:08:38,861
He drove a delivery truck.

264
00:08:39,041 --> 00:08:42,257
Joan scrubbed other people's floors for her.

265
00:08:42,608 --> 00:08:44,361
Nineteen eighty-seven.

266
00:08:44,541 --> 00:08:45,690
Kim's wedding.

267
00:08:45,870 --> 00:08:48,215
Joan wrote, I wasn't invited.

268
00:08:48,395 --> 00:08:50,383
I drove to Cleveland anyway,

269
00:08:50,383 --> 00:08:52,867
and I parked across the street from

270
00:08:52,867 --> 00:08:55,280
the church, and I watched her come

271
00:08:55,280 --> 00:08:56,557
out on Dale's arm.

272
00:08:56,737 --> 00:08:58,188
She was so beautiful.

273
00:08:58,368 --> 00:09:00,005
I hope he's good to her.

274
00:09:00,185 --> 00:09:03,378
I drove home before anybody saw me.

275
00:09:03,558 --> 00:09:05,789
And Kim told me she put her

276
00:09:05,789 --> 00:09:07,277
face in her hands,

277
00:09:07,277 --> 00:09:09,012
on that closet floor,

278
00:09:09,012 --> 00:09:11,739
and she sobbed until the sun came

279
00:09:11,739 --> 00:09:11,987
up.

280
00:09:12,337 --> 00:09:13,384
In the morning,

281
00:09:13,384 --> 00:09:15,198
Kim drove to the hospital,

282
00:09:15,198 --> 00:09:17,571
and she called me from the parking

283
00:09:17,571 --> 00:09:18,339
lot, honey.

284
00:09:18,519 --> 00:09:21,059
I'd been sitting with Joan for two

285
00:09:21,059 --> 00:09:21,433
days.

286
00:09:21,613 --> 00:09:23,262
I met her in the hallway.

287
00:09:23,442 --> 00:09:24,814
She was fifty-two,

288
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:26,491
with gray in her hair,

289
00:09:26,491 --> 00:09:30,380
holding the nineteen seventy-five diary against her

290
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:30,837
chest.

291
00:09:31,017 --> 00:09:32,776
She said, Aunt Ruth,

292
00:09:32,776 --> 00:09:33,920
did you know?

293
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:35,406
And I said,

294
00:09:35,406 --> 00:09:37,188
no, sweetheart.

295
00:09:37,368 --> 00:09:38,866
Nobody knew.

296
00:09:39,046 --> 00:09:40,799
Joan made sure of it.

297
00:09:40,979 --> 00:09:43,208
And Kim walked into that room.

298
00:09:43,558 --> 00:09:46,459
Joan was lying there with her eyes

299
00:09:46,459 --> 00:09:49,873
closed, with tubes and wires everywhere.

300
00:09:50,053 --> 00:09:52,364
And Kim sat down beside the bed

301
00:09:52,364 --> 00:09:53,706
and took her hand,

302
00:09:53,706 --> 00:09:56,538
that old, rough hand that scrubbed all

303
00:09:56,538 --> 00:09:57,507
those floors.

304
00:09:57,687 --> 00:09:58,910
And she said,

305
00:09:58,910 --> 00:10:01,263
Joan, I read the diaries.

306
00:10:01,443 --> 00:10:03,150
I know about my mother.

307
00:10:03,330 --> 00:10:05,176
I know about the floors.

308
00:10:05,356 --> 00:10:06,958
I know about the church.

309
00:10:07,138 --> 00:10:09,198
And then she said a word she

310
00:10:09,198 --> 00:10:11,479
had never, ever said to Joan in

311
00:10:11,479 --> 00:10:12,362
forty years.

312
00:10:12,542 --> 00:10:13,773
She said, Mom.

313
00:10:13,953 --> 00:10:15,604
I'm so sorry,

314
00:10:15,604 --> 00:10:16,112
Mom.

315
00:10:16,463 --> 00:10:18,897
And Joan's fingers moved,

316
00:10:18,897 --> 00:10:19,481
honey.

317
00:10:19,661 --> 00:10:21,832
I saw it with my own eyes.

318
00:10:22,012 --> 00:10:25,100
Her fingers closed around Kim's hand.

319
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:27,882
The nurse came running when the monitor

320
00:10:27,882 --> 00:10:28,415
changed.

321
00:10:28,595 --> 00:10:30,354
And two days later,

322
00:10:30,354 --> 00:10:32,299
Joan opened her eyes.

323
00:10:32,479 --> 00:10:35,013
The first thing she saw was Kim,

324
00:10:35,013 --> 00:10:36,596
asleep in the chair,

325
00:10:36,596 --> 00:10:40,080
with that nineteen seventy-five diary on her

326
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:40,397
lap.

327
00:10:40,577 --> 00:10:42,758
And Joan couldn't talk yet,

328
00:10:42,758 --> 00:10:44,536
because of the stroke.

329
00:10:44,716 --> 00:10:47,072
So she just looked at her,

330
00:10:47,072 --> 00:10:47,978
and cried.

331
00:10:48,329 --> 00:10:49,564
Later that week,

332
00:10:49,564 --> 00:10:52,344
honey, Kim asked me the question I'd

333
00:10:52,344 --> 00:10:53,425
been dreading.

334
00:10:53,605 --> 00:10:55,101
She said, Aunt Ruth,

335
00:10:55,101 --> 00:10:57,344
why didn't Daddy ever tell me?

336
00:10:57,524 --> 00:10:58,422
And I said,

337
00:10:58,422 --> 00:11:02,017
sweetheart, I think your father was ashamed.

338
00:11:02,197 --> 00:11:04,948
Ashamed that he couldn't keep your mother.

339
00:11:05,128 --> 00:11:07,341
And he let Joan carry that for

340
00:11:07,341 --> 00:11:10,069
him, because she was stronger than he

341
00:11:10,069 --> 00:11:10,364
was.

342
00:11:10,544 --> 00:11:12,923
Kim said, she was stronger than all

343
00:11:12,923 --> 00:11:13,331
of us.

344
00:11:13,511 --> 00:11:14,736
And I said,

345
00:11:14,736 --> 00:11:15,961
yes, honey.

346
00:11:16,141 --> 00:11:17,267
She still is.

347
00:11:17,617 --> 00:11:20,530
Kim took Joan home to Cleveland that

348
00:11:20,530 --> 00:11:23,201
December, sweetheart, to recover.

349
00:11:23,381 --> 00:11:25,837
She turned her own dining room into

350
00:11:25,837 --> 00:11:26,539
a bedroom.

351
00:11:26,719 --> 00:11:28,599
And on Christmas morning,

352
00:11:28,599 --> 00:11:32,962
Kim's children, Joan's step-grandchildren she'd never been

353
00:11:32,962 --> 00:11:34,165
allowed to meet,

354
00:11:34,165 --> 00:11:37,249
climbed into her bed with their presents.

355
00:11:37,429 --> 00:11:39,933
Joan's speech came back slowly,

356
00:11:39,933 --> 00:11:41,307
over that winter.

357
00:11:41,487 --> 00:11:44,277
And the first full sentence she said,

358
00:11:44,277 --> 00:11:45,181
Kim told me,

359
00:11:45,181 --> 00:11:47,519
was, I always wanted to be your

360
00:11:47,519 --> 00:11:48,046
mother.

361
00:11:48,397 --> 00:11:50,154
Joan is eighty-three now,

362
00:11:50,154 --> 00:11:52,263
honey, and she lives with Kim.

363
00:11:52,443 --> 00:11:54,649
And every night before bed,

364
00:11:54,649 --> 00:11:57,101
she still writes one page in a

365
00:11:57,101 --> 00:11:58,654
little cloth diary.

366
00:11:58,834 --> 00:12:01,213
But now, Kim reads it the next

367
00:12:01,213 --> 00:12:02,879
morning, over coffee,

368
00:12:02,879 --> 00:12:04,465
with her permission.

369
00:12:04,645 --> 00:12:07,321
Kim says she's catching up on forty

370
00:12:07,321 --> 00:12:07,780
years.

371
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:09,478
And last Christmas,

372
00:12:09,478 --> 00:12:11,396
Kim gave Joan a present.

373
00:12:11,576 --> 00:12:13,676
A brand-new cloth diary,

374
00:12:13,676 --> 00:12:15,602
and on the first page,

375
00:12:15,602 --> 00:12:17,439
in Kim's handwriting,

376
00:12:17,439 --> 00:12:18,577
it said, Mom.

377
00:12:18,757 --> 00:12:21,311
You can tell me everything now.

378
00:12:21,661 --> 00:12:24,495
Here's what I want you to remember,

379
00:12:24,495 --> 00:12:24,981
honey.

380
00:12:25,161 --> 00:12:27,727
Sometimes the person you blame the most

381
00:12:27,727 --> 00:12:30,095
is the one who's been protecting you

382
00:12:30,095 --> 00:12:30,885
the longest.

383
00:12:31,065 --> 00:12:32,770
Tell me in the comments,

384
00:12:32,770 --> 00:12:36,037
sweetheart, is there someone you misjudged for

385
00:12:36,037 --> 00:12:36,463
years?

386
00:12:36,643 --> 00:12:39,020
There are more of my family's stories

387
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:41,267
in the playlist right there on your

388
00:12:41,267 --> 00:12:41,717
screen.

389
00:12:41,897 --> 00:12:42,837
Good night.

390
00:12:43,017 --> 00:12:44,515
Merry Christmas.
